          "text": "Nice — let's lock in your prediction before I spoil it. There's one subtlety here (the direction of the second fold), so I'd like your reasoning too.\n\n```openui lifecycle=ephemeral id=paper-fold-layers-guess\n\nroot = LearningSurface([guess], \"Paper strip: how many layers?\", \"Your guess and reasoning come before my answer.\", \"ephemeral\")\nguess = Question([\n  { header: \"Your guess\", question: \"A strip of paper is folded in half once, then in half again. How many layers of paper are there at the end?\", type: \"choice\", choices: [\"2 layers\", \"4 layers\", \"8 layers\", \"16 layers\"], allowText: true, hint: \"Guess first — then tell me why.\" },\n  { header: \"How you folded\", question: \"For the second fold, what did you do with the strip?\", type: \"choice\", choices: [\"Folded it in half again the same way (lengthwise, making it quarter-length)\", \"Folded it across the width, perpendicular to the first fold\", \"It depends / other\", \"I haven't decided yet\"], hint: \"The two folds can be made in different directions.\" },\n  { header: \"Reasoning\", question: \"In a sentence or two, explain how you arrived at your layer count.\", type: \"text\", hint: \"How does each fold multiply the layers?\" }\n], \"ephemeral\", \"Folding and layers\", \"Give the number, the fold direction, and your reasoning.\")\n```\n\n"
